{
  "schemaVersion": "1.0",
  "scriptId": "avg-01-average-basics-sum-count",
  "sourceType": "MANUAL",
  "metadata": {
    "title": "Average Basics: Equal Share, Total and Missing Values",
    "description": "See an average as an equal share, move quickly between mean and total, and recover missing values or counts.",
    "teachingApproach": "Open with an equal-share story so the formula has meaning. Move through the three interchangeable forms Average, Total and Count; then use them for a missing observation, two-number and ratio problems, common transformations of every value, and finally a partial-change capstone where the total must be updated carefully. Each skill gets a worked example, fresh practice and a parallel retry.",
    "targetDurationMinutes": 28,
    "sourceScope": "Teach Average = Sum ÷ Number through an equal-share picture, then reverse it to Sum = Average × Number and Number = Sum ÷ Average. Use direct lists, missing observations, two-number and ratio-based averages, and simple unknown-count questions. Show that changing every observation by the same addition, subtraction or multiplication changes the mean in the same way. Finish with a capstone where only part of a data set changes, so the learner must update the total rather than blindly shift the mean. Every answer should be checked by rebuilding the total."
  },
  "startNodeId": "start",
  "nodes": {
    "start": {
      "id": "start",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Let's make average feel like one simple idea instead of a formula to memorise.\n\nAn average is the value everyone would have if the total were shared equally. Once that picture is clear, missing-number questions become much easier.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1": {
      "id": "teach_1",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Suppose four friends have 8, 10, 12 and 14 marbles. Together they have 44.\n\nIf the 44 marbles were shared equally, each friend would get 11.\n\nThat equal-share value is the average.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1_step": {
      "id": "teach_1_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Average = total ÷ number of observations.\n\nHere:\n44 ÷ 4 = 11\n\nThe average does not have to be one of the original values. It is the level everyone would have after an equal share.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_1"
        }
      ]
    },
